WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:19.763
(HORSES WHINNY)

3
00:00:25.162 --> 00:00:27.369
Do not stop until you reach Tartarus

4
00:00:27.498 --> 00:00:29.671
The horses will run
until their hearts give out.

5
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.906
Hyperion will soon have the Bow. Leave.

6
00:00:48.452 --> 00:00:50.125
(PANTING)

7
00:00:55.426 --> 00:00:57.406
(FOOTSTEPS RUMBLING)

8
00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.306
Forgive me. Father. Forgive me.

9
00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.539
I only broke the law
to protect the mortal.

10
00:01:18.382 --> 00:01:21.659
(SLOW-MOTION SHOUT)

11
00:01:47.912 --> 00:01:51.086
No god will ever again come to your aid.

12
00:01:52.416 --> 00:01:54.089
You are on your own!

13
00:01:56.721 --> 00:01:59.395
Do you understand. mortal?

14
00:02:00.558 --> 00:02:03.004
I have faith in you. Theseus.

15
00:02:03.728 --> 00:02:07.642
Prove me right.

16
00:02:08.232 --> 00:02:09.768
Lead your people.

17
00:02:21.579 --> 00:02:23.320
(SCREECHING)

18
00:02:51.842 --> 00:02:52.946
Halt!

19
00:02:54.412 --> 00:02:56.722
(HORSES SNORTING. PANTING)

20
00:03:03.888 --> 00:03:05.367
(SNARLING)

21
00:03:10.094 --> 00:03:12.074
The horse I prayed for when I was a boy.

22
00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:13.902
What is wrong with him?

23
00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:17.804
They're dying.

24
00:03:39.657 --> 00:03:41.728
Where are the men?

25
00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:43.930
MAN: They have yet to return. sire.

26
00:03:44.795 --> 00:03:47.139
What does the sight
of the bird tell you?

27
00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.368
Speak.

28
00:03:54.238 --> 00:03:55.376
The gods.

29
00:03:57.775 --> 00:03:59.584
They came from above.

30
00:04:00.211 --> 00:04:01.656
The gods?

31
00:04:01.779 --> 00:04:04.419
They appeared and laid waste
to the men. my king.

32
00:04:07.151 --> 00:04:08.425
The gods.

33
00:04:11.288 --> 00:04:12.528
The gods.

34
00:04:13.591 --> 00:04:16.663
They protected the slave
who travels with the oracle.

35
00:04:20.231 --> 00:04:23.041
The gods fight on their behalf. sire.

36
00:04:28.372 --> 00:04:30.875
If the men hear of this.
there will be panic.

37
00:04:32.042 --> 00:04:34.818
I know. I know.

38
00:04:37.214 --> 00:04:38.693
(SQUISHING)

39
00:04:38.816 --> 00:04:40.887
(SCREAMING CONTINUES)

40
00:05:23.027 --> 00:05:26.167
ATHENA: In peace. sons bury their fathers.

41
00:05:27.631 --> 00:05:31.078
In war. fathers bury their sons.

42
00:05:38.876 --> 00:05:40.685
Are we at war. Father?

43
00:06:08.572 --> 00:06:10.609
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

44
00:06:21.885 --> 00:06:23.831
I have important information
for the council.

45
00:06:23.954 --> 00:06:25.126
Theseus.

46
00:06:25.756 --> 00:06:27.463
I know this man. Let him through.

47
00:06:33.631 --> 00:06:35.474
I hope you've come to join the fight.

48
00:06:48.612 --> 00:06:49.955
Where's the army?

49
00:06:59.957 --> 00:07:01.698
Tell me about the slave.

50
00:07:04.862 --> 00:07:07.035
He's from your village. is he not?

51
00:07:08.899 --> 00:07:10.708
- Answer me!
- Yes.

52
00:07:12.236 --> 00:07:14.079
He was a peasant.

53
00:07:18.375 --> 00:07:20.150
As was I.

54
00:07:21.145 --> 00:07:23.125
Forgive me. Your Majesty.

55
00:07:23.247 --> 00:07:25.488
- I meant no...
- Quiet.

56
00:07:25.616 --> 00:07:27.994
And his family?

57
00:07:28.118 --> 00:07:32.533
His mother was raped by some villagers.
Nobody would many her.

58
00:07:35.159 --> 00:07:36.604
He was a bastard.

59
00:07:36.727 --> 00:07:38.729
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

60
00:07:41.098 --> 00:07:42.441
And his name?

61
00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.404
Theseus.

62
00:07:45.402 --> 00:07:47.609
Very well. I'll meet him.

63
00:07:58.015 --> 00:08:00.996
Helios tells me you have information
that could be of use to us.

64
00:08:01.118 --> 00:08:03.394
Hyperion is in possession
of the Epirus Bow.

65
00:08:04.922 --> 00:08:07.402
- The Epirus Bow?
- Yes. it's a weapon forged by Heracles.

66
00:08:07.558 --> 00:08:10.232
Oh. please. I heard the same stories
you did as a child.

67
00:08:10.361 --> 00:08:14.707
There are gods living in the clouds.
Titans buried in the rocks.

68
00:08:14.832 --> 00:08:19.804
Listen. I was a disbeliever just like
you are. But the Epirus Bow exists

69
00:08:19.937 --> 00:08:25.182
I understand there are many Hellenics
who put faith in the myths and the gods.

70
00:08:25.309 --> 00:08:28.051
but we on the Hellenic council do not.

71
00:08:28.178 --> 00:08:31.057
They are metaphors. son. Nothing more.

72
00:08:31.181 --> 00:08:35.095
We are a society of laws
based on negotiation and reason.

73
00:08:35.219 --> 00:08:38.530
If you try and negotiate with Hyperion.
you will be the death of us all.

74
00:08:38.655 --> 00:08:41.636
If I were to accept your counsel.

75
00:08:41.759 --> 00:08:44.399
Theseus from Kolpos. what would it be?

76
00:08:44.528 --> 00:08:47.065
Seal the gates and prepare for war.

77
00:08:47.197 --> 00:08:49.370
We have Hoplite battalions returning.
We can't seal the gate.

78
00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:53.414
No one will return! We are the last!

79
00:08:53.537 --> 00:08:55.915
I'm sure you'll understand
if I don't accept the advice

80
00:08:56.039 --> 00:08:59.384
of an alluring palm reader
and her peasant lover.

81
00:09:01.044 --> 00:09:03.217
Sir. a Heraklion envoy approaches.

82
00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:11.028
There. you see? No ruler wishes for war.

83
00:09:11.155 --> 00:09:15.103
They only wish to be taken seriously
at the bargaining table.

84
00:09:15.926 --> 00:09:18.338
Alert the council. Prepare a delegation.

85
00:09:22.599 --> 00:09:23.669
MAN: Bows!

86
00:09:27.905 --> 00:09:28.906
HELIOS: Stop!

87
00:09:32.042 --> 00:09:36.457
Stop! Remain still.
or we'll be forced to fire upon you.

88
00:09:40.651 --> 00:09:42.392
Extend your arms outward.

89
00:09:46.256 --> 00:09:48.258
He bears the olive branch of peace.

90
00:09:49.593 --> 00:09:54.269
HYPERION: My king wishes to speak
to the one called Theseus from Kolpos.

91
00:09:58.569 --> 00:09:59.912
Theseus.

92
00:10:02.406 --> 00:10:04.977
Hyperion's envoy
desires a word with you.

93
00:10:06.443 --> 00:10:10.289
Like the vision.
he sends for you with arms open.

94
00:10:11.782 --> 00:10:13.887
Seeking an embrace of loyalty.

95
00:10:14.017 --> 00:10:15.690
Phaedra.

96
00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.627
Have you never been wrong?

97
00:10:31.935 --> 00:10:33.642
We can't protect you beyond this gate.

98
00:10:40.777 --> 00:10:42.415
I am Theseus!

99
00:10:42.946 --> 00:10:45.950
Come closer. I have a message for you.

100
00:10:46.884 --> 00:10:47.954
Don't risk it.

101
00:10:52.756 --> 00:10:54.360
At worst. you lose a peasant.

102
00:11:04.635 --> 00:11:07.241
- Better?
- Uh-huh. Yes.

103
00:11:08.872 --> 00:11:10.852
Why do you cover your face?

104
00:11:10.974 --> 00:11:13.716
All are equal in Hyperion's midst.

105
00:11:13.844 --> 00:11:17.155
I myself am only a vessel
for his demands. Nothing more.

106
00:11:18.248 --> 00:11:21.718
- And he asks me by name?
- Indeed he does.

107
00:11:21.852 --> 00:11:23.263
And how does he know it?

108
00:11:23.387 --> 00:11:26.129
There's little the king does not know.

109
00:11:26.256 --> 00:11:28.463
He knows that you have no father.

110
00:11:28.592 --> 00:11:31.869
And like him. you were cast aside
by your own people.

111
00:11:31.995 --> 00:11:33.668
Does he know of my rage?

112
00:11:35.098 --> 00:11:38.511
Does he know that I live only to see
his blood at the end of my sword?

113
00:11:38.635 --> 00:11:40.672
Does he know he butchered my mother?

114
00:11:48.845 --> 00:11:52.952
Now that he's seen your face. he knows.

115
00:12:02.326 --> 00:12:03.669
You wouldn't make it.

116
00:12:04.928 --> 00:12:06.407
Coward!

117
00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.339
Embrace me. Theseus.

118
00:12:09.466 --> 00:12:12.538
They will never give you a seat
at their table

119
00:12:12.669 --> 00:12:14.444
but you could sit at the head of mine.

120
00:12:15.839 --> 00:12:21.084
Long after this war is over. my mark
will be left on this world forever.

121
00:12:23.647 --> 00:12:27.322
The sun will never set
on my blood. Theseus.

122
00:12:27.451 --> 00:12:31.126
This is what I offer you. Immortality.

123
00:12:32.289 --> 00:12:35.532
Deeds are eternal. Not the flesh.

124
00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:43.504
The gods may be on your side.
but tomorrow...

125
00:12:44.835 --> 00:12:46.542
I unleash the Titans.

126
00:12:51.208 --> 00:12:52.710
What was discussed?

127
00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.587
Seal the gate.

128
00:12:55.712 --> 00:12:58.818
- What were his demands?
- Seal the gate.

129
00:12:59.983 --> 00:13:01.587
HYPERION: Theseus.

130
00:13:04.054 --> 00:13:05.863
Ahh...

131
00:13:07.824 --> 00:13:09.326
(SHOUTS)

132
00:13:18.201 --> 00:13:21.205
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

133
00:13:28.011 --> 00:13:31.151
- That was him. wasn't it?
- I was that close.

134
00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.959
I don't know if I can do
what Zeus asks of me.

135
00:14:09.653 --> 00:14:12.031
By doubting one
comes the truth. Theseus.

136
00:14:16.793 --> 00:14:18.272
The gods chose well.

137
00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:09.976
Sir. there's movement on the front.

138
00:16:33.697 --> 00:16:35.370
What is he holding?

139
00:16:38.635 --> 00:16:39.670
The Bow.

140
00:16:56.686 --> 00:16:59.826
MAN: The commanders
are all dead! Fall back!

141
00:16:59.956 --> 00:17:01.560
(PANICKED SHOUTING)

142
00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:08.741
Hold! Stand your ground!

143
00:17:09.332 --> 00:17:11.744
Hold! Stand your ground!

144
00:17:24.447 --> 00:17:25.790
Listen to me!

145
00:17:29.286 --> 00:17:30.458
Listen!

146
00:17:33.857 --> 00:17:37.964
- Who are you to tell us what to do?
- I am nobody to tell you what to do!

147
00:17:38.094 --> 00:17:41.507
I am Theseus. a common man! One of you!

148
00:17:41.631 --> 00:17:45.135
I share your blood!
And I share your fear!

149
00:17:46.036 --> 00:17:51.179
But to run now would offer our souls
and the souls of our children

150
00:17:51.308 --> 00:17:53.015
to a terrible darkness!

151
00:17:56.579 --> 00:17:58.718
(ALL SHOUTING)

152
00:18:02.786 --> 00:18:05.630
Hold! We must stand and fight!

153
00:18:06.156 --> 00:18:09.968
Their numbers count for nothing
in the tunnel! Stand your ground!

154
00:18:12.295 --> 00:18:15.538
Stand your ground!
Who are they that we are not?

155
00:18:18.201 --> 00:18:21.671
Just because they scald their faces
and scar their bodies...

156
00:18:22.439 --> 00:18:25.977
does not mean they are braver
or stronger than we are.

157
00:18:26.676 --> 00:18:27.950
They are cowards!

158
00:18:28.812 --> 00:18:30.314
They hide behind their masks.

159
00:18:31.014 --> 00:18:34.791
They are human.
and they bleed like you and I.

160
00:18:41.157 --> 00:18:42.500
Listen to me!

161
00:18:43.593 --> 00:18:45.038
Stand your ground!

162
00:18:45.895 --> 00:18:47.772
Fight for honor!

163
00:18:47.897 --> 00:18:49.638
Fight for the man beside you!

164
00:18:49.766 --> 00:18:52.076
Fight for the mothers who bore you!

165
00:18:52.202 --> 00:18:53.772
Fight for your children!

166
00:18:53.903 --> 00:18:55.348
Fight for your future!

167
00:18:56.039 --> 00:18:57.575
Fight so your name survives!

168
00:18:59.075 --> 00:19:00.053
Fight...

169
00:19:01.011 --> 00:19:02.957
for immortality!

170
00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:13.058
Let us write history
with Heraklion blood!

171
00:19:15.025 --> 00:19:17.027
(FOOTSTEPS RUMBLING)

172
00:19:21.064 --> 00:19:23.772
Ready! Move!

173
00:19:58.835 --> 00:19:59.643
(SHOUTS)

174
00:20:08.812 --> 00:20:11.554
(ALL GRUNTING. SHOUTING)

175
00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:49.025
King Hyperion.

176
00:20:50.453 --> 00:20:53.798
We can negotiate. I see no reason...

177
00:21:04.033 --> 00:21:06.035
HYPERION: Theseus!

178
00:21:07.137 --> 00:21:10.482
Here I am! Theseus of Kolpos!

179
00:21:14.177 --> 00:21:16.384
- Where's your king?
- He is no king.

180
00:21:34.197 --> 00:21:34.902
(SHOUTS)

181
00:21:38.268 --> 00:21:39.474
Stavros! The shrine!

182
00:22:03.526 --> 00:22:05.665
Theseus! I'm right behind you!

183
00:22:22.946 --> 00:22:24.289
Phaedra!

184
00:22:27.250 --> 00:22:28.957
Phaedra!

185
00:22:29.085 --> 00:22:30.428
Stay in the shrine.

186
00:23:02.485 --> 00:23:03.657
Hyperion!

187
00:23:11.294 --> 00:23:13.001
(SNARLING)

188
00:23:15.765 --> 00:23:16.869
No!

189
00:23:38.955 --> 00:23:40.559
(GRUNTS)

190
00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:42.033
STAVROS (MUFFLED):
Theseus. wake up!

191
00:23:47.797 --> 00:23:49.105
Theseus!

192
00:23:52.669 --> 00:23:53.977
Theseus!

193
00:24:03.813 --> 00:24:05.258
(GROANS)

194
00:24:14.824 --> 00:24:16.098
Theseus!

195
00:24:17.660 --> 00:24:19.003
I got the Bow!

196
00:24:19.896 --> 00:24:21.375
Stavros.

197
00:24:23.099 --> 00:24:25.841
I got the Bow.
Get out of here while you can!

198
00:24:27.837 --> 00:24:28.907
I'll hold them off!

199
00:24:29.038 --> 00:24:30.244
Stavros.

200
00:24:30.373 --> 00:24:33.445
Go now! I got the Bow!

201
00:24:33.576 --> 00:24:35.078
I'll hold them off while I can!

202
00:24:35.211 --> 00:24:38.215
- Get out of here! Go!
- (CREATURES SNARLING)

203
00:24:43.286 --> 00:24:45.425
Which one of you are coming with me?

204
00:24:51.794 --> 00:24:53.774
(SCREAMING)

205
00:25:15.618 --> 00:25:18.064
None of you will leave this place.

206
00:25:19.922 --> 00:25:21.868
(SHOUTS)

207
00:25:32.902 --> 00:25:34.142
Leave here!

208
00:25:35.338 --> 00:25:37.284
This is no longer your fight.

209
00:25:39.509 --> 00:25:40.852
Find Hyperion.

210
00:25:45.014 --> 00:25:47.585
(ALL SNARLING)

211
00:25:52.088 --> 00:25:54.932
(GODS GRUNTING)

212
00:26:14.310 --> 00:26:15.186
(GASPS)

213
00:26:24.587 --> 00:26:26.328
(GRUNTING)

214
00:26:28.524 --> 00:26:31.130
(BOTH SCREAMING)

215
00:26:32.662 --> 00:26:34.505
(BOTH GRUNTING)

216
00:27:02.892 --> 00:27:04.462
(GROANING)

217
00:27:05.595 --> 00:27:07.768
(PANTING)

218
00:27:17.306 --> 00:27:18.979
Die with your gods.

219
00:27:28.951 --> 00:27:30.988
(BOTH SHOUTING)

220
00:27:55.611 --> 00:27:57.352
(SNARLING)

221
00:28:02.885 --> 00:28:04.762
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

222
00:28:28.644 --> 00:28:30.954
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

223
00:28:36.052 --> 00:28:37.429
(GRUNTING)

224
00:28:41.691 --> 00:28:43.967
(SHOUTING)

225
00:28:50.933 --> 00:28:53.243
(ALL SHOUTING)

226
00:29:08.384 --> 00:29:09.863
(SHOUTING)

227
00:29:36.345 --> 00:29:37.790
Athena!

228
00:29:48.024 --> 00:29:49.867
(GROANING)

229
00:30:07.543 --> 00:30:08.681
Father!

230
00:30:11.814 --> 00:30:13.657
Don't forsake mankind.

231
00:30:46.282 --> 00:30:47.659
(GRUNTING)

232
00:31:26.655 --> 00:31:27.963
(SIGHS)

233
00:31:36.899 --> 00:31:38.845
What does it feel like. knowing...

234
00:31:40.870 --> 00:31:43.248
knowing that there'll
be no memory of you?

235
00:31:45.374 --> 00:31:46.717
I have won.

236
00:31:48.944 --> 00:31:52.414
My death will make me a legend.

237
00:31:52.548 --> 00:31:54.585
(PANTING)

238
00:32:01.624 --> 00:32:02.967
My deeds...

239
00:32:05.161 --> 00:32:07.437
will go down in history.

240
00:32:13.969 --> 00:32:15.949
I'm writing your history.

241
00:32:16.972 --> 00:32:18.280
(ROARS)

242
00:32:18.407 --> 00:32:19.351
(SCREAMS)

243
00:32:19.475 --> 00:32:21.785
(BOTH GRUNTING)

244
00:32:35.024 --> 00:32:37.664
(SCREAMING)

245
00:32:42.765 --> 00:32:44.540
Do it!

246
00:32:56.512 --> 00:32:58.219
(MEN SHOUTING)

247
00:33:01.617 --> 00:33:07.329
This... is our last embrace. Hyperion.

248
00:33:09.758 --> 00:33:10.759
Look at me.

249
00:33:12.728 --> 00:33:14.207
Look at me.

250
00:33:16.665 --> 00:33:17.837
I'm the last thing...

251
00:33:19.468 --> 00:33:20.879
you will ever see.

252
00:33:25.207 --> 00:33:28.677
Witness hell.

253
00:33:29.078 --> 00:33:31.024
(STABBING SOUND)

254
00:33:33.849 --> 00:33:35.522
(GURGLING)

255
00:33:40.956 --> 00:33:43.095
(FADING GROAN)

256
00:35:03.172 --> 00:35:05.482
(ALL SHOUTING)

257
00:35:24.960 --> 00:35:26.803
(SHOUTING. RUMBLING FADES)

258
00:35:50.652 --> 00:35:54.327
<i>OLD MAN: All men's
souls are immortal.</i>

259
00:35:57.459 --> 00:36:03.466
<i>But the souls of the righteous
are immortal and divine.</i>

260
00:36:07.936 --> 00:36:10.712
<i>Once a faithless man.</i>

261
00:36:10.839 --> 00:36:15.254
<i>Theseus gave his life
to save mankind</i>

262
00:36:15.377 --> 00:36:17.755
<i>and earned a place amongst the gods.</i>

263
00:36:21.016 --> 00:36:24.395
<i>They rewarded his
bravery with a gift.</i>

264
00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:27.865
<i>A son. Acamas.</i>

265
00:36:50.746 --> 00:36:52.589
(ARMIES SHOUTING)

266
00:36:53.315 --> 00:36:54.658
(GASPS)

267
00:36:59.521 --> 00:37:02.525
Don't be afraid of your visions.
little one.

268
00:37:04.326 --> 00:37:06.670
- What's your name?
- Acamas.

269
00:37:07.296 --> 00:37:09.037
Acamas.

270
00:37:10.332 --> 00:37:12.312
A strong name.

271
00:37:15.270 --> 00:37:19.844
I knew your father.
He was a very brave man.

272
00:37:23.579 --> 00:37:27.527
Soon. it will be your time

273
00:37:29.351 --> 00:37:30.955
My time for what?

274
00:37:31.086 --> 00:37:33.999
The fight against evil
never ends. Acamas.

275
00:37:34.123 --> 00:37:36.933
War is coming to the heavens.

276
00:37:38.327 --> 00:37:43.504
And your father will be there.
fighting for your future.

277
00:37:46.468 --> 00:37:47.469
PHAEDRA: Acamas.

278
00:37:48.137 --> 00:37:49.207
Acamas.

279
00:37:57.546 --> 00:37:59.025
Who was that. son?

280
00:37:59.715 --> 00:38:00.750
Just...

281
00:38:03.418 --> 00:38:04.920
Just an old man.

